      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,3)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.4, & \\,x=2 \\\\ 0.6, & \\,x=4 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=3]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,3)$ is shown above.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=3] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,3) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.4+4\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =3.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
